==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Trixi the Revenant''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
With her very frequent multi-hit attacks, she has decent DPS against her target traits despite her seemingly low attack power. However, it is necessary to keep in mind that her usage may be limited in some circumstances due to her short range of 280.

Trixi works in a much different way compared to many existing crowd-controllers with [[Freeze]]. She has a very short Freeze time of only a third of a second, but she attacks very frequently and therefore has many chances to Freeze. Because of this, her 50% chance to Freeze is much more consistent compared to other units with the same chance such as [[Snow Miku 2021 (Uber Rare Cat)|Snow Miku 2021]]. The result is that her Freezes act as continuous stuns to enemies with an expected uptime of 64.7%. This nature of her Freeze ability allows her to significantly delay attacks from target traits, especially if they have a slow attack frequency or even just a long foreswing. She also works well against enemies with more knockbacks, as it will be easier for her to knock them back before they have a chance to attack.

Finally, her immunities help her tank and stay in the frontline, as her HP stat is made more impressive with her Strong ability working against 3 traits. Slow, Warp and Curse are all nice immunities for a tanker. However, her 4 knockbacks can still limit her with high-DPS enemies who outrange her or otherwise avoid her freeze, and her range means that she does not really benefit from frequently repositioning.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Tanker}}

