==Trivia==
*When first added to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]'s files, Trixi's descriptions initially said that she was "Strong vs [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]], ''[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]'' and [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]". This error was fixed before she became obtainable. However the change introduced a new typo, in that "[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]" is not pluralized.
*Her three targeted traits may represent the past (Relic), present (Traitless) and future (Alien).
*She and [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Bad Blaster Saki]] share similar hairstyles, Strong Against abilities (albeit only as a [[Talents|Talent]] in Saki's case) and Alien and Relic targets. Like many of the [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]], she also uses futuristic technology.
*She is the first [[:Category:Gacha Cats|Gacha Cat]] that does not target all or all but one trait to [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|Target Relic]] enemies in her Normal and Evolved Forms.
*She and [[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Agent Staal]] are tied for the fastest attack rate of all Cats by technicality, as the previous record-holder [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] attacks three times in 18 frames, while they attack 3 times in 17 frames.
*Muranyasa is a reference to 16th-century swordsmith [[wikipedia:Muramasa|Muramasa]] combined with にゃん ''nyan'' (meow) or にゃんこ ''nyanko'' (kitty).
*Trixi the Revenant's 10-year coma is a reference to her releasing during the [[Anniversary/10th Year|10th Anniversary]] for the English, Korean and Taiwanese versions.
**Despite the fact that she was released during the [[Anniversary/12th Year|12th Anniversary]] in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], her description still says that her coma was only 10 years.
*According to the descriptions of Trixi the Revenant and Agent Staal, Trixi was betrayed by Staal.

